# Op4_DrawFrame (the draw tail of every Op4_Draw* op and anim frame op; never called, so the cases
# run at Op4_DrawKillSidesBelow's first call: an a4 object being drawn, a6 = it, d4/d5 = its x/y;
# that object shows frame 0, handle $8000, which holds no art). Ruling 5, step 2: each case builds
# the frame-swap state named below. Reachability of each is undetermined after cov8-cov16 (NOTES,
# Open questions: "Spr_ChangeFrame's cross-table equal handles", "ArtCache_Acquire" / "Spr_SwapFrameArt",
# cov12's and cov16's entries); none contradicts what those entries established.
at $00677E

# The new frame from Tbl_1DDB60 (ROM, >= 0) and the old one from the RAM frame table (negative,
# indexed from g_ArtRelRingWr) naming the same handle, so nothing is swapped ($006854). The only
# RAM frames whose handle a ROM frame shares are the Hatter road bank's (Op6_InitBankFrames at
# FC40: frame $FEB6 has handle $8080, its entry at $A764 - $14A = $A61A), and the ROM frames with
# handle $8080 are $000A-$00A0 (cov16_shared.py): which draw sources can show both on one object is
# not established (cov16), so the pair is the one the data allows.
case shared_rom_new
w a6 + $1E = $000A
w a6 + $20 = $FEB6
w $FFFFA61A = $8080

# The same pair the other way round: a RAM new frame and a ROM old frame on one handle ($006886).
case shared_ram_new
w a6 + $1E = $FEB6
w a6 + $20 = $000A
w $FFFFA61A = $8080

# No art descriptor free with blocks to spare ($0068E2): the pickup effect Scr4_0132B2's two-frame
# animation ($2AB2 -> $2ABC, handles $86EA / $86EC: the old art resident with this object its one
# user, descriptor $AA4A refcount $FF; the new one not resident) with g_ArtDescsFree 0
# and g_ArtBlocksFree $40, as 007F5E.syn's no_descriptor: ArtCache_Init's 50 descriptors count
# cached art too, and 50 one-block arts resident or cached use them all; the swap fails and the
# old frame stays. Not seen in the corpus (the blocks-short path next to it, $0068E6, is).
case no_descriptor
w a6 + $20 = $2AB2
w a6 + $1E = $2ABC
w $FFFF86EA = $AA4A
b $FFFFAA4A = $FF
b $FFFFAA4B = 1
w $FFFFAA4C = 0
b $FFFFA770 = $40
b $FFFFA772 = 0

# The new frame's art resident with refcount $80, i.e. 128 users ($006906: the decrement to $7F is
# undone). A descriptor's count is 0 (cached) or minus its users; a positive byte is cleared by the
# release that makes it, so only $80 gets here: 128 objects showing one art. Not bounded (cov12:
# the most frame words that can name one art, the $8C-block pool plus HUD and weapon slots).
case users_128
w a6 + $20 = $2AB2
w a6 + $1E = $2ABC
w $FFFF86EA = $AA4A
b $FFFFAA4A = $FF
b $FFFFAA4B = 1
w $FFFFAA4C = 0
w $FFFF86EC = $AA44
b $FFFFAA44 = $80
b $FFFFAA45 = 1
w $FFFFAA46 = 0

# The old frame's release finding its art with no user ($006916-$00691A: the raised refcount is
# positive and cleared again): the change to frame 0 from $2AB2 whose handle holds a cached
# descriptor $AA44 (refcount 0, on the release ring). The state of 008000.syn / 007F5E.syn's
# release_cached: after a bank is loaded over a handle in use (007EB8.syn), an old sprite's release
# takes a new user's count to 0 and the new user's own release finds 0.
case release_cached
w a6 + $20 = $2AB2
w a6 + $1E = 0
w $FFFF86EA = $AA44
b $FFFFAA44 = 0
b $FFFFAA45 = 1
w $FFFFAA46 = $8F00
